From dbcb54c57074056dc59ae2008ca2355dd5aee009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 20:38:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v1.6.0: hardening pass + full i18n

- rtrafd: cache the three per-tick nvram reads in write_live (30->3/s),
  open-once sysfs pread for the WAN counters, resolve top-talker MAC once
  when the row is built, NULL-check all 83 ring allocs; Reaper_Traffic
  Live per-device/network/top tables throttled to ~1 Hz
- rmcpd: fix popen_pid fd + zombie-child leak when fdopen fails after fork
- httpd/web.c: sanitize rmcp_client into the newline-delimited session
  file (strip CR/LF, dotted-quad only)
- rc/services.c: validate lan_ifname before splicing it into iptables
- rc/watchdog.c: correct the acsd async-cooldown comment
- Reaper_Advisor: saveSettings() now sends http_id and checks the response
  instead of reporting success unconditionally; Refresh button regrouped
  next to the title
- Login/Logout: use the Reaper favicon (/favicon.ico)
- SLOP: drop the never-fired QoS mode-link branch; strand checkPolicy() as
  a no-op stub
- i18n: tokenize remaining hardcoded strings (16 new keys + reuse of stock
  keys), add a truncate+hover-tooltip helper (.rtip) to both rails, and a
  full 24-language translation of the 384 Reaper dict keys (machine-assisted,
  pending native review)
